  "$comment": "VR2-00 route/state fixture manifest. Every VR2 ticket names ONE ordinary product runtime route and its state(s). A design-system specimen (Grundlagen/Foundations, Gallery, registry), Storybook, a unit test surface, or a deep-only / hidden prototype route is NOT an accepted consumer and is listed under `specimenRoutes` so the evidence gate can reject it. Viewports and locales are the standing gate requirement; reducedMotion:true is additionally required where the ticket owns motion. Routes are logical names for the state-driven app (there is no path router); the `entry` field records the ordinary way a user reaches the state from a cold portfolio.",
